[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 457,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 370,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65026,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 392,
        "headingId": 370,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Adenocarcinoma of Skene gland origin is an adenocarcinoma arising in the Skene glands, morphologically and immunohistochemically similar to prostatic adenocarcinoma.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-08T17:12:52"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 458,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 371,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65027,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 392,
        "headingId": 371,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>8140/3 Carcinoma of Skene, Cowper, and Littr&eacute; glands</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-08T17:12:52"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 459,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 372,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65028,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 392,
        "headingId": 372,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>2C71.0 &amp; XH22Z8 Adenocarcinoma of vagina &amp; Carcinoma of Skene, Cowper, and Littr&eacute; glands</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-08T17:12:52"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 460,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 373,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65029,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 392,
        "headingId": 373,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Acceptable:</em> Skene or periurethral gland adenocarcinoma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-08T17:12:52"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 461,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 374,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65030,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 392,
        "headingId": 374,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-08T17:12:52"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 462,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 375,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65031,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 392,
        "headingId": 375,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Periurethral/paraurethral, urethral, anterior vaginal wall, and posterior bladder neck {2990157; 14668555; 9584326; 7525428; 3114949; 28872768; 7507278; 20870432}</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-08T17:12:52"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 463,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 376,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65032,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 392,
        "headingId": 376,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The usual presentation is with a mass and (less frequently) haematuria or incontinence. Serum PSA may be elevated {2990157; 14668555; 20870432; 7525428}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-08T17:12:52"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 464,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 377,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65033,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 392,
        "headingId": 377,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>This extremely rare tumour has been reported in patients ranging in age from 46 to 88&nbsp;years (median: 70&nbsp;years) {2990157; 14668555; 9584326; 7525428; 3114949; 28872768; 7507278; 20870432}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-08T17:12:52"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 465,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 378,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65034,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 392,
        "headingId": 378,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-08T17:12:52"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 466,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 379,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65035,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 392,
        "headingId": 379,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>These tumours arise from the periurethral Skene glands, the female equivalent of the prostatic glands in males.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-08T17:12:52"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 473,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 386,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65036,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 392,
        "headingId": 386,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>It is a polypoid or flat tumour, 1.0&ndash;3.5&nbsp;cm in size {7525428}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-08T17:12:52"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 467,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 380,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65037,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 392,
        "headingId": 380,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>These neoplasms are usually morphologically similar to acinar prostatic adenocarcinoma. Typically, there is a population of well-formed to poorly formed glands lined by cuboidal or columnar epithelium, with pale or eosinophilic cytoplasm, round nuclei, and prominent nucleoli. A cribriform pattern is common, and individual glands, solid areas, or a single-file pattern can be seen. The degree of nuclear atypia is variable. Goblet cells are rarely seen. Residual benign Skene glands may be present. Immunohistochemically, usual Skene gland adenocarcinoma is positive for prostatic markers: PSA, PAP, NKX3-1, P501S, AMACR, and PIN4 cocktail (high-molecular-weight cytokeratin, p63, and AMACR) {2990157; 14668555; 9584326; 7525428; 3114949; 28872768; 7507278; 20870432}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-08T17:12:52"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 468,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 381,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65038,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 392,
        "headingId": 381,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-08T17:12:52"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 469,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 382,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65039,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 392,
        "headingId": 382,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-08T17:12:52"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 472,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 385,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65040,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 392,
        "headingId": 385,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> adenocarcinoma morphologically resembling a prostatic adenocarcinoma.</p>\r\n<p><em>Desirable:</em> positivity for prostatic markers.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-08T17:12:52"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 470,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 383,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65041,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 392,
        "headingId": 383,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The staging is the same as for other urethral neoplasms.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-08T17:12:52"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 471,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 384,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 65042,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 392,
        "headingId": 384,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Experience with this neoplasm is limited; a single case has been reported with metastases involving inguinal lymph nodes.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-08T17:12:52"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]